This similarity is particularly interesting because it suggests that the two automated approaches encounter comparable difficulties when interpreting place names without sufficient geographical context. For example, Catonsville in Baltimore appears twice in the automated LLM method and four times in the automated spaCy and geopy method. Although repeated references can be legitimate, they can also produce an exaggerated impression of spatial concentration if they are not distinguished from separate geographical locations.


